From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:50:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: chips-media: add the WAVE420L HEVC encoder of the
 Sophgo SG2000

The SG2000 has a Chips&Media WAVE420L HEVC encoder. Its host interface
is the WAVE4 one: the boot and remap registers are the WAVE5 ones, but
the commands and the command registers are different.

Add a V4L2 mem2mem encoder: NV12 in, HEVC Main out, at constant QP,
with an IDR picture every GOP. The secondary AXI (the codec SRAM) is not
used. The driver loads the vendor firmware, monet.bin.

The register sequence follows Sophgo's vendor driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
